    "note": "This narrative uses US National Archives records of Parks’s arrest, Library of Congress materials including Parks’s own accounts and boycott documents, and US National Park Service history of earlier challenges. It distinguishes municipal law, routine practice, and subsequent collective organizing. No imagined interior monologue or dialogue is supplied. The case is not presented as the first or only act of resistance.",
