    "question": "When the law makes being found dangerous, is hiding a choice—or the smallest freedom left?",
    "note": "This account is anchored in Jacobs's 1861 autobiographical narrative, North Carolina state historical records, and the Digital Public Library of America's curated primary-source set. The memoir is a first-person source with literary shaping, not a transcript of every event. No invented conversation or interior scene is added.",
